      "id": 1,
      "text": "Zephyrhills began as Abbott in 1888, renamed Abbott Station in 1896 when the railroad depot opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://mainstreetzephyrhills.org/our-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1910, Captain Jeffries formalized Abbott Station as the City of Zephyrhills, honoring Civil War veterans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://mainstreetzephyrhills.org/our-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Zephyrhills Public Library, founded in 1912, joined the Pasco County Library Cooperative and got a new building in 2014.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zephyrhills%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zephyrhills’ name reflects its rolling topography, with “Zephyr” meaning a gentle west wind and “hills” describing the landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zephyrhills%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city hosts an annual Founders Day celebration each March, celebrating its founding and community spirit.",
